Agar aapke paas very large table (in GBs) hai jisme live data insert ho raha hai, aur aapko 2 saal purana data delete karna hai, to direct DELETE query karna dangerous ho sakta hai:

Lock lag sakta hai table par.

Performance impact ayega.

Disk I/O high ho sakta hai.

Long-running transaction se rollback heavy hoga.

✅ Safe and Efficient Ways to Delete Old Data
🔹 1. Batch-wise Delete (Most Recommended)
Instead of deleting all old data in one go, delete it in small batches.

🔧 Example (MySQL):
sql
Copy
Edit
-- Repeat this in a loop/scheduler
DELETE FROM big_table
WHERE created_date < NOW() - INTERVAL 2 YEAR
LIMIT 10000;
Har 10,000 records delete karo.

Repeat until all old data is gone.

You can use a script (e.g., Python, Java, shell script) or SQL procedure with delay between batches.

🔹 2. Use Partitioning (Best for Future Scalability)
If table ka size hamesha badhta ja raha hai, use table partitioning (by created_date) so you can drop old partitions instantly.

🔧 Example (MySQL Partitioning):
sql
Copy
Edit
PARTITION BY RANGE (YEAR(created_date)) (
    PARTITION p2020 VALUES LESS THAN (2021),
    PARTITION p2021 VALUES LESS THAN (2022),
    ...
);
🔥 Then:
sql
Copy
Edit
ALTER TABLE big_table DROP PARTITION p2021;
Very fast, almost instant.

No row-level deletion, just metadata update.

🔹 3. Create a New Table and Swap
If deleting takes too long, create a new table with only required (recent) data.

🔧 Steps:
Create new table new_big_table.

Copy recent data:

sql
Copy
Edit
INSERT INTO new_big_table SELECT * FROM big_table WHERE created_date >= NOW() - INTERVAL 2 YEAR;
Rename tables:

sql
Copy
Edit
RENAME TABLE big_table TO old_table, new_big_table TO big_table;
Drop old table later.

Note: Ensure no writes happen during swap or you must handle sync.

🧠 Bonus Tips
Create index on created_date for faster deletion.

Do deletes during off-peak hours.

Monitor locks and slow queries if on live DB.

✅ Summary
| Method                | Speed     | Safe for Live DB | Complexity     |
| --------------------- | --------- | ---------------- | -------------- |
| `DELETE` with batch   | Medium    | ✅ Yes            | Low            |
| Partition + DROP      | Very Fast | ✅ Yes            | Medium         |
| Copy to new table     | Fast      | ⚠️ Careful       | Medium         |
| Direct `DELETE` (all) | ❌ Slow    | ❌ No             | Easy but risky |
